SDL 2.32.10 (Android): closing an OpenSL ES output while the activity is paused.

close_audio_device() marks the device shut down and then joins its audio thread; the driver has no say before the
join. OpenSL ES's audio thread waits in openslES_WaitDevice for a buffer to finish playing: SDL_SemWait on playsem,
which only the buffer-queue callback posts. While the activity is paused, Android_PumpEvents_Blocking has set the
player to SL_PLAYSTATE_PAUSED (openslES_PauseDevices), so no buffer finishes and nothing posts the semaphore: a
close from another thread while the app is in the background hangs until the app comes back to the front.
OpenSL ES is SDL's first Android driver, so this is the output every stream without a chosen output gets.
Measured on the SHIELD TV 2026-10-16: switching the app off during a stream left the session worker in
LiStopConnection -> SS4S_PlayerAudioClose -> SDL_CloseAudioDevice -> SDL_WaitThread, the audio thread (SDLAudioP2)
in SDL_SemWait, and the host streaming to the frozen app until its own timeout ~3.7 minutes later.

openslES_WaitDevice now waits in 100 ms slices and returns once the device is shutting down. SDL_RunAudio checks
shutdown at the top of its loop; a buffer the paused player refuses posts the semaphore itself (openslES_PlayDevice),
so the thread drains what it holds and leaves. While the device is open and not closing, nothing changes.
Capture (openslES_CaptureFromDevice) waits the same way; Eclipse does not capture on Android, so it is left alone.

--- a/src/audio/openslES/SDL_openslES.c
+++ b/src/audio/openslES/SDL_openslES.c
@@ -630,8 +630,13 @@
 
     LOGV("openslES_WaitDevice()");
 
-    /* Wait for an audio chunk to finish */
-    SDL_SemWait(audiodata->playsem);
+    /* Wait for an audio chunk to finish -- or for the device to close. While the activity is paused the player is
+     * paused too (openslES_PauseDevices), no chunk finishes, and close_audio_device joins this thread. */
+    while (SDL_SemWaitTimeout(audiodata->playsem, 100) == SDL_MUTEX_TIMEDOUT) {
+        if (SDL_AtomicGet(&this->shutdown)) {
+            return;
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 static void openslES_PlayDevice(_THIS)
